# configure-effects: crash-reproduction path -
# Configure > Effect volume > Enter > Esc (deterministic). Exercises the Effect-volume popup
# (showAdjustOptions) that used to smash the stack (fixed in 715098c).
#
# enter, then shot:menu: reach the main menu and confirm it with a
#   screenshot instead of a trailing Esc (see menu.keys for why Esc is no
#   longer used to normalize onto the main menu itself, and why one Enter
#   -- not two -- is the measured-reliable count here).
# down/enter: Multiplayer Race is disabled, so one Down from the default
#   "Start Racing" selection lands on "Configure" (skip-disabled behaviour,
#   verified in the original trial); Enter opens it.
# down/enter: Configure's items are Music Volume / Effect Volume / Define
#   Keyboard / Define Gamepad-Joystick / Gamepad-Joystick Disabled /
#   Previous menu - one Down from the default "Music Volume" lands on
#   "Effect Volume"; Enter opens the popup.
# wait, enter, esc: the exact repro - sit on the popup, confirm, leave
#   Configure back to the main menu. This Esc is inside the Configure
#   submenu ("Previous menu"), not on the main menu itself, so the
#   main-menu Esc finding (see menu.keys) does not apply to it.
#
# Verified with screenshots with the Esc-free prefix: reaches "ADJUST
# EFFECT VOLUME: NN%", then returns to the main menu with Configure
# highlighted, no crash (the bug is fixed).
# Three Enters, as in results-orig.keys: the port now shows dr.exe's two
# publisher splashes (Apogee, then rmd.bmp) after its own intro animation, like the
# original, so the single Enter measured for the port before no longer
# reaches the main menu.
enter w3000
enter w3000
enter w3500
shot:menu
down w800
enter w1500
down w800
enter w1500
w3000
enter w1500
esc w1200
